# ── Docker build context excludes ────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared by every service that builds from the repo root (context: ..):
# apps/web/Dockerfile (which does `COPY . .`), backend/Dockerfile.cpu, and the
# self-host backend/Dockerfile (GPU). Without these excludes the context is
# ~1.7GB — dominated by the .git history of binary demo files, host-installed
# node_modules, and Next.js build output — making every deploy slow and baking
# junk (and the transient .env secrets) into image layers.
#
# Do NOT exclude backend/vendor: the GPU image COPYs backend/vendor/LAM.
# Do NOT exclude apps/web/public: it holds the demo .splattie files we serve.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Version control
.git
**/.git

# Node deps + Next.js output (reinstalled via `npm ci` and rebuilt in-image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next

# Python caches / virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Local runtime data (analytics db lives in the backend-data volume, not the image)
backend/data

# Secrets — the deploy writes a transient 0600 .env at the repo root for
# compose interpolation; it must never reach a build layer. (.env.example stays.)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Test / tooling output + OS cruft
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
